\newlabel{tab:livemem}{{9}{7}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Paired differences of the live runs of Table\nobreakspace  {}8\hbox {} in the duo's accuracy (points), $A - B$ on the same images: mean $\pm $ standard error over visits, and the number of visits in which $A$ is better. Held-out: the visits of the two rotations pooled (32); test: the three seeds averaged per visit (15 visits). Visits are not independent (a collapse carries into the next visit; the two rotations hold the same images in another order), so the standard error is a noise floor, not a confidence interval. Computed by \texttt  {scripts/41\_paired\_comparisons.py}.}}{7}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:paired}{{10}{7}}
